    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d676">

                <pb facs="0614" n="498" xml:id="pg498"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 123.R27/64.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé d’Affaires at
                            London to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1121.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-12-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 15, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have the sad duty of announcing to you that the Ambassador died today at
                    Dorchester House, at ten minutes past twelve o’clock.</p>
                <p>Subject to your instructions, I have assumed control of the Embassy as Chargé
                    d’Affaires.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Irwin B. Laughlin.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
